            <title>[LU-21228] lfs find --report: statistics about what a search finds</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21228</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Add &lt;tt&gt;--report&lt;/tt&gt; to &lt;tt&gt;lfs find&lt;/tt&gt;, so that any search can describe what it finds instead of (or as well as) listing it: counts, histograms of file size, allocated space, space beyond the size, directory entries, name length, links and the age of each time, and the largest directories by entries and by bytes. The output is one YAML document in the style of &lt;tt&gt;job_stats&lt;/tt&gt;, readable as it stands and parsed by any YAML parser.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It works on every kind of search:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;a target scan (&lt;tt&gt;-&lt;del&gt;device&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;&lt;/del&gt;&lt;del&gt;target&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;&lt;/del&gt;&lt;del&gt;fsname&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;&lt;/del&gt;-local&lt;/tt&gt;), which reports both what it read (&lt;tt&gt;scanned&lt;/tt&gt;) and what the options matched (&lt;tt&gt;matched&lt;/tt&gt;); a sweep reads its OSTs first, so each file's allocated space is the sum of its objects;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;a client walk, which stats each size the MDT did not return, or takes lazy SOM with &lt;tt&gt;--lazy&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;lfs find --device /dev/sdb --report                  # report saved, path on stderr
lfs find --fsname testfs -size +1G --report=big.yaml  # one file for the filesystem
lfs find /mnt/testfs/proj -user bob --report=-        # YAML on stdout
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;-&lt;del&gt;report&lt;span class="error"&gt;&amp;#91;=FILE&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/tt&gt; is an action, as &lt;tt&gt;-fprint&lt;/tt&gt; is in find(1); &lt;tt&gt;&lt;/del&gt;&lt;del&gt;no-report&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;&lt;/del&gt;&lt;del&gt;report-format=yaml&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;&lt;/del&gt;-report-memory=SIZE&lt;/tt&gt; go with it. &lt;tt&gt;llapi_find_report()&lt;/tt&gt; gives programs the same report; with &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21206" title="LFU: keep the scan API private for 2.18" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-21206"&gt;LU-21206&lt;/a&gt; this public interface may become internal, reached through &lt;tt&gt;llapi_find()&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;struct find_param&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Asked for by Andreas Dilger after the lfu-stats prototype (github.com/scopedog/lfu-stats). Still to agree: a report saved by default on every target scan, repeated &lt;tt&gt;--device&lt;/tt&gt;, and merging reports from separate runs.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
